items.source:
Return the <a href="../../interceptor/CacheResolver.html" title="interface in org.springframework.cache.interceptor"><code>CacheResolver</code></a> bean to use to resolve exception caches for
annotation-driven cache management. Implementations must explicitly declare
<a href="../../../context/annotation/Bean.html" title="annotation interface in org.springframework.context.annotation"><code>@Bean</code></a>, for example,
<pre class="code">@Configuration
@EnableCaching
public class AppConfig implements JCacheConfigurer {
    @Bean // important!
    @Override
    public CacheResolver exceptionCacheResolver() {
        // configure and return CacheResolver instance
    }
    // ...
}
</pre>
See <a href="../../annotation/EnableCaching.html" title="annotation interface in org.springframework.cache.annotation"><code>EnableCaching</code></a> for more complete examples.

